  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Complete small gracile horn-bearing male ungulate with multiple cranial appendages. Do not reduce to skull or use Synthetoceras Y horn. [\"2021 study identifies males by cranial ornamentation and separates female and crushed incomplete male measurements. Do not extrapolate exact full body dimensions from damaged male.\", \"1892 appendage illustrations are original specimen drawings, soft tissue coverage is not directly preserved. Use understated skin-covered shapes without invented horn rings.\", \"Whole-body lengths, tail, ears and coat are conservative reconstruction choices. No copy of other species body mesh or artwork.\", \"Historical paper used Lower Miocene dating; use current Oligocene context from later study rather than historical date terminology.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"skull_length_m\": 0.215, \"basis\": \"Osborn/Wortman1892p356 male skull occipital condyle to premaxillary tip215mm, facial region130mm. Different specimens:2021 femaleAMNH1229 measured20.75cm; maleAMNH53523 incomplete18.8cm NOT full length.\", \"body_length_m\": 1.0, \"shoulder_height_m\": 0.6, \"whole_size_status\": \"Illustrative small gracile sheep-sized body reconstruction, not directly measured articulated skeleton.\"}",
    "zh": "原创低多边形研究；形态、尺度及不确定性严格以本次已核参考为界。原始限定：Complete small gracile horn-bearing male ungulate with multiple cranial appendages. Do not reduce to skull or use Synthetoceras Y horn. [\"2021 study identifies males by cranial ornamentation and separates female and crushed incomplete male measurements. Do not extrapolate exact full body dimensions from damaged male.\", \"1892 appendage illustrations are original specimen drawings, soft tissue coverage is not directly preserved. Use understated skin-covered shapes without invented horn rings.\", \"Whole-body lengths, tail, ears and coat are conservative reconstruction choices. No copy of other species body mesh or artwork.\", \"Historical paper used Lower Miocene dating; use current Oligocene context from later study rather than historical date terminology.\"] {\"unit\": \"meter\", \"skull_length_m\": 0.215, \"basis\": \"Osborn/Wortman1892p356 male skull occipital condyle to premaxillary tip215mm, facial region130mm. Different specimens:2021 femaleAMNH1229 measured20.75cm; maleAMNH53523 incomplete18.8cm NOT full length.\", \"body_length_m\": 1.0, \"shoulder_height_m\": 0.6, \"whole_size_status\": \"Illustrative small gracile sheep-sized body reconstruction, not directly measured articulated skeleton.\"}"
  },
